Why don't you finally go to sleep?

00:36:36.520 --> 00:36:38.520
Everyone has to be fresh on his post tomorrow morning.

00:36:38.720 --> 00:36:40.660
What do you think of the restart?

00:36:41.160 --> 00:36:47.700
What can I say?

00:36:48.280 --> 00:36:51.890
I'm happy, of course.

00:36:53.270 --> 00:36:53.730
Aren't you?

00:37:00.000 --> 00:37:06.220
I have a little problem in the engine section. I'll be back in five minutes.

00:37:35.560 --> 00:37:37.520
I'm going to sleep now, Elie. Good night's sleep.

00:37:37.660 --> 00:37:44.530
Oh, I accidentally broke the screen. Please turn it back on.

00:37:44.910 --> 00:37:46.700
It's okay, Zuko. Good night.

00:38:00.000 --> 00:38:15.550
F, sorry to wake you up. Bad news.

00:38:16.320 --> 00:38:19.040
A manned probe of the Tsunro people has started a reconnaissance flight.

00:38:19.660 --> 00:38:21.940
How should I behave? Should it land in emergency?

00:38:22.260 --> 00:38:23.680
Or do I have to ask only for topic 3?

00:38:24.200 --> 00:38:25.560
In which direction?

00:38:26.560 --> 00:38:27.860
Exactly where it's not supposed to go.

00:38:27.920 --> 00:38:28.820
Get down.

00:38:30.000 --> 00:38:31.540
But what if something goes wrong again?

00:39:15.040 --> 00:39:15.560
So no crash.

00:39:16.260 --> 00:39:16.940
Vehicles there.

00:39:17.220 --> 00:39:19.050
Turn off the landing station immediately.

00:42:54.060 --> 00:42:55.400
The Pima are not allowed to see you.

00:42:55.520 --> 00:42:56.950
We are glad that you have come.

00:42:57.350 --> 00:42:58.020
Who are you?

00:42:58.100 --> 00:42:59.410
How do you know that we have landed?

00:43:09.850 --> 00:43:10.490
Quick, he has to go!

00:43:10.690 --> 00:43:24.020
We are Turi, this is our planet!

00:43:24.260 --> 00:43:25.020
Quick, you have to go!

00:44:36.810 --> 00:44:37.170
The effect.

00:44:37.330 --> 00:44:44.130
The effect.

00:44:44.470 --> 00:44:44.650
Yeah.

00:45:00.000 --> 00:45:07.960
last time I saw him. He called back later and I

00:45:07.960 --> 00:45:15.350
wished him good night. Please try to remember exactly what he

00:45:15.350 --> 00:45:20.540
said last time. He apologized that he had

00:45:20.540 --> 00:45:23.920
crashed and asked me to switch it on again. That's

00:45:24.230 --> 00:45:27.400
how he could fly away unnoticed with the probe. But why? And

00:45:28.800 --> 00:45:29.040
where to?

00:45:33.900 --> 00:45:36.880
Hmm, he didn't agree with our restart.

00:45:37.700 --> 00:45:43.510
Now he forces us to stay here, at least until we find him.

00:45:48.300 --> 00:45:53.080
But how will the Thema react when they notice that he's taking a trip?

00:45:53.560 --> 00:45:58.540
What a crazy idea.

00:45:58.990 --> 00:45:59.290
I'm sorry.

00:46:00.000 --> 00:46:07.420
We will find out soon. There comes the bus, or whatever you call it. Maybe they'll bring Succo.

00:46:30.000 --> 00:46:36.620
I come to pick you up.

00:46:36.620 --> 00:46:40.200
As I said, for a visitation program.

00:46:40.660 --> 00:46:41.960
Have you noticed anything about Suko's trip?

00:46:44.090 --> 00:46:46.480
Rall, you stay here. Maybe Suko will report.

00:46:46.880 --> 00:46:48.210
We'll be back in two to three hours.

00:46:49.010 --> 00:46:54.330
What is the purpose of your flight?

00:46:54.570 --> 00:46:56.990
A flight to prepare for our return.

00:46:57.350 --> 00:46:58.330
Did you take a picture?

00:47:00.440 --> 00:47:09.120
Young friend, I'm really sorry, but I don't have as much time as my men.

00:47:09.240 --> 00:47:10.240
I can't talk to you for hours.

00:47:47.468 --> 00:47:49.828
There, on this chair, everyone is chatting with me.

00:48:07.740 --> 00:48:09.740
Can you understand what I'm saying?

00:48:17.468 --> 00:48:20.288
I will now ask you a few very simple questions.

00:48:20.476 --> 00:48:23.636
And you each have five seconds for your answer.

00:48:23.996 --> 00:48:24.496
Sure.

00:48:35.720 --> 00:48:37.280
What was the purpose of your flight?

00:48:37.640 --> 00:48:39.160
The flight was to prepare for our return.

00:48:39.520 --> 00:48:43.320
But why so fast? You always have five seconds for your answer.

00:48:46.690 --> 00:48:56.820
Hahaha, so once again, what was the purpose of her flight?

00:49:00.510 --> 00:49:01.890
The flight attendant is preparing for take-off.

00:49:01.950 --> 00:49:12.420
Have you taken aerial shots?

00:49:13.060 --> 00:49:19.360
The aerial camera is out of order.

00:49:19.500 --> 00:49:22.460
Have you taken aerial shots?

00:49:23.080 --> 00:49:25.900
You have five seconds to answer.

00:49:26.540 --> 00:49:29.940
You have five seconds to answer.

00:49:30.250 --> 00:49:34.420
You have five seconds for your answer!

00:49:34.760 --> 00:49:43.860
Stop, we want to go with you.

00:49:44.510 --> 00:49:45.990
The boss wants to speak to the commander alone.

00:49:47.410 --> 00:49:48.950
There's a little tip for you.

00:49:49.030 --> 00:49:49.410
Please?

00:49:50.640 --> 00:49:55.480
Kalle won't have an easy time.

00:51:33.452 --> 00:51:35.452
Subtitles by Stephanie Geiges

00:51:54.380 --> 00:51:55.380
Please take your seats.

00:51:59.084 --> 00:51:59.984
Don't be afraid.

00:52:01.440 --> 00:52:05.700
She is very poisonous, but she obeys the word.

00:53:35.690 --> 00:53:37.210
Sometimes I play with it for hours.

00:53:37.830 --> 00:53:41.560
Don't you want to try it too?

00:53:42.260 --> 00:53:45.880
The game partner is worth gold.

00:53:46.220 --> 00:53:56.090
I'm afraid our party last night...

00:53:56.090 --> 00:53:58.570
...or was it before yesterday...

00:53:58.570 --> 00:53:59.900
...had you...

00:54:00.000 --> 00:54:03.940
I had terrible headaches.

00:54:12.960 --> 00:54:16.280
It's hard to guess the wishes of guests who come from so far away.

00:54:16.740 --> 00:54:25.250
I hope you'll treat me to breakfast.

00:54:40.040 --> 00:54:54.120
Very. And one of the women didn't come along.

00:54:54.240 --> 00:54:56.270
There were four of them at the party.

00:54:57.590 --> 00:54:59.850
Wait a minute. I see a way to clear the room.

00:55:00.000 --> 00:55:00.260
to take the ship in hand.

00:55:00.900 --> 00:55:03.360
Can you fly this Synro probe?

00:55:05.360 --> 00:55:06.000
I think so.

00:55:06.220 --> 00:55:13.980
In the meantime, treat him a little with music.

00:55:14.270 --> 00:55:16.230
If he doesn't tell anything, he should also forget what he saw.

00:55:30.540 --> 00:55:50.400
Here's the thing. We didn't ask anyone for help.

00:55:50.600 --> 00:55:53.340
The reason for your long journey is illusory.

00:55:53.540 --> 00:55:56.140
You assured that you would prepare your return.

00:55:56.820 --> 00:55:59.540
It amazes me that one of your people...

00:56:00.000 --> 00:56:04.430
I hope you will carry out an exploration flight across our planet without her consent.

00:56:04.730 --> 00:56:08.720
May I know where our friend is?

00:56:11.480 --> 00:56:13.660
I'm used to getting my questions answered first.

00:56:13.840 --> 00:56:17.240
You haven't asked any questions so far.

00:56:17.320 --> 00:56:27.700
You must have noticed long ago that we came here on a peaceful note.

00:56:30.030 --> 00:56:34.150
And they also know that we have to try to restart the meeting according to the agreement.

00:56:36.950 --> 00:56:39.950
Only with mutual trust.

00:56:40.680 --> 00:56:49.550
I bent my nose a bit, but the two of them rolled me back on the legs.

00:56:50.010 --> 00:56:56.950
I had to make an emergency landing. Some effect.

00:56:57.290 --> 00:56:58.530
We can't continue the conversation now.

00:57:00.920 --> 00:57:02.660
I have to take care of my crew first.

00:57:02.820 --> 00:57:12.840
Where is Tronk?

00:57:12.840 --> 00:57:14.870
We don't know!

00:57:15.090 --> 00:57:15.910
Answer, you coward!

00:57:16.030 --> 00:57:16.490
Where is Tronk?

00:57:16.490 --> 00:57:17.810
He flew with the Chimros to the spaceship today!

00:57:18.090 --> 00:57:28.480
A.I.N.S.T.I.N.S.

00:57:28.680 --> 00:57:29.380
O.M.I.E.T.

00:57:41.290 --> 00:57:43.670
You got us into trouble with your idea of an excursion.

00:57:43.990 --> 00:57:46.510
Be glad that Akala isn't here, she's pretty angry.

00:58:00.000 --> 00:58:00.500
Are you dumb?

00:58:35.760 --> 00:58:37.960
Stay in the sun and close the hatch immediately!

00:59:00.790 --> 00:59:22.000
I'm sorry, I'm sorry.

00:59:22.000 --> 00:59:22.760
I'm sorry, I'm sorry.

00:59:36.360 --> 00:59:39.420
Did you just make a little nod or why are you letting us get away with it?

00:59:40.580 --> 00:59:42.380
Throw my look at the Hangar monitor.

00:59:42.740 --> 00:59:44.490
The prisoner.

00:59:44.770 --> 00:59:47.750
The hero.

01:00:04.990 --> 01:00:05.690
This Lumpen.

01:00:05.690 --> 01:00:27.620
Come out, but don't be stupid.

01:00:30.150 --> 01:00:41.180
We now know how people are interrogated by you.

01:00:41.260 --> 01:00:46.810
You allow me to ask you a question in our own way.

01:00:47.090 --> 01:00:55.350
Is it true that you were supposed to bring back our probe, which was in emergency, and hand it over to us?

01:00:56.580 --> 01:00:59.270
I... I'm glad...

01:01:00.000 --> 01:01:02.640
If you... if you understand our order this way.

01:01:02.940 --> 01:01:07.270
There is a vehicle outside that you will bring back.

01:01:08.780 --> 01:01:10.940
Tell your boss he should leave his tricks.

01:01:11.360 --> 01:01:15.670
We will leave in 36 hours. Come on.

01:01:38.860 --> 01:01:42.660
He's trying to remind her of something, but he can't do it.

01:01:43.260 --> 01:01:47.230
He's... he's mentally blocked.

01:01:47.670 --> 01:01:50.180
I don't think there's another explanation for his behavior.

01:01:52.430 --> 01:01:53.230
Mentally blocked?

01:01:56.190 --> 01:01:59.470
Listen, Mül, when I was at...

01:02:00.320 --> 01:02:06.900
I suddenly had the feeling that I couldn't think of what I actually wanted.

01:02:07.040 --> 01:02:07.620
It was...

01:02:07.620 --> 01:02:07.980
Wait a minute.

01:02:08.590 --> 01:02:09.410
Everything in order.

01:02:09.710 --> 01:02:13.840
As far as I know, for example, ultrasound can mentally block in hard dosage.

01:02:14.560 --> 01:02:16.410
Out of fear of pain.

01:02:16.710 --> 01:02:20.330
But you haven't been treated with ultrasound at all.

01:02:20.670 --> 01:02:23.560
I even injected a strong dose of chlorine.

01:02:24.160 --> 01:02:27.700
If it's about a pain blockade, it should be lifted.

01:02:29.420 --> 01:02:29.860
But...

01:02:30.000 --> 01:02:30.820
Do you think it's possible to have an acoustic influence?

01:02:31.860 --> 01:02:32.420
No.

01:02:33.020 --> 01:02:35.540
Then let's try something optical.

01:02:37.070 --> 01:02:38.450
I found it in the special recording.

01:02:40.720 --> 01:02:42.580
Maybe you can help his memory.

01:03:14.400 --> 01:03:15.080
Only one more.

01:03:15.160 --> 01:03:15.500
There!

01:03:17.410 --> 01:03:17.650
Ui!

01:03:29.470 --> 01:03:29.830
Zuko!

01:03:30.000 --> 01:03:30.540
It's your planet!

01:03:30.740 --> 01:03:31.060
Succo!

01:03:31.200 --> 01:03:31.600
Your planet!

01:03:32.000 --> 01:03:32.460
Calm down, Succo!

01:03:32.580 --> 01:03:38.120
I'll make sure he sleeps 24 hours, then we'll see.

01:03:38.460 --> 01:03:46.810
It can be that not only Succo, but also we others, that we are all mentally blocked.

01:03:48.640 --> 01:03:52.500
If that's the case, there must be something that we can't think of, can't pronounce.

01:03:53.630 --> 01:03:55.850
So we haven't spoken out since we've been blocked.

01:03:56.290 --> 01:03:59.810
Our computer would have to figure it out.

01:04:00.000 --> 01:04:01.160
if you compare our conversations.

01:04:01.720 --> 01:04:02.340
Cheap.

01:04:30.350 --> 01:04:31.230
Is there a possibility?

01:04:33.410 --> 01:04:37.400
Yes, there is, but the effect only occurs after 24 hours of sleep.

01:05:00.060 --> 01:05:05.800
If you really come, then you have to go alone through the entrance hatch, and then we have you.

01:05:06.670 --> 01:05:09.850
No, completely wrong. We'll let you in here unhindered.

01:05:11.140 --> 01:05:14.640
That's the only way we can find out who is in contact with you by the Tories.

01:05:15.040 --> 01:05:16.480
Maybe there are already a few leaders.

01:05:17.000 --> 01:05:29.000
You are directly above us with a manned and three small unmanned probes. Go!

01:07:41.160 --> 01:07:43.460
These little lunks are careful. They got wind.

01:07:44.500 --> 01:07:46.120
Then get the cosmonauts here.

01:07:46.460 --> 01:07:48.070
Maybe the Turidans will get up.

01:08:18.940 --> 01:08:19.660
Come to me, no matter what!

01:09:16.412 --> 01:09:18.412
Let's go, quickly to our vehicles!

01:09:30.000 --> 01:09:37.220
Quick! He's bleeding heavily.

01:09:51.010 --> 01:09:52.390
He has to go to our doctor right away.

01:09:52.690 --> 01:09:53.050
Go!

01:10:00.000 --> 01:10:02.080
Second sondag is coming. It's four o'clock.

01:10:32.520 --> 01:10:34.440
Take the turrets, or we'll let you get away!

01:10:34.680 --> 01:10:40.160
Order from Ronk, attack!

01:11:01.600 --> 01:11:03.740
Don't come near us. They can't get us back.

01:11:04.080 --> 01:11:13.030
Energy back?

01:11:13.330 --> 01:11:14.260
Not yet.

01:11:14.460 --> 01:11:19.050
When the vehicles start, you'll start with full speed.

01:11:19.310 --> 01:11:21.750
I don't think they can fix their weapons so quickly.

01:11:23.100 --> 01:11:23.780
What about you?

01:11:25.060 --> 01:11:25.760
That's an order.

01:11:34.636 --> 01:11:36.636
Our second Sunday is coming.

01:12:08.480 --> 01:12:09.960
A series of beautiful successes.

01:12:10.800 --> 01:12:13.200
First, the successful crash.

01:12:13.720 --> 01:12:15.880
Second, the successful handbrake.

01:12:16.020 --> 01:12:18.750
And the planned reception in the workshop.

01:12:19.340 --> 01:12:23.720
Oh yes, one thing you forgot to report.

01:12:24.020 --> 01:12:28.700
How you came to the pretty little hut.

01:12:30.030 --> 01:12:32.100
A joke of the Zynro people.

01:12:32.870 --> 01:12:36.070
You can also build an invisible shield around your sun.

01:12:36.190 --> 01:12:39.590
And you tested this shield with your head.

01:12:40.270 --> 01:12:44.960
Or did you want to use the two turbis?

01:12:45.620 --> 01:12:48.000
...who had escaped.

01:12:49.410 --> 01:12:50.950
Maybe escaping is too negative.

01:12:51.650 --> 01:12:53.670
The thing with the shield was not to be foreseen.

01:12:53.770 --> 01:12:56.990
The planned attack of our vehicles on the probe was a smooth failure.

01:13:00.540 --> 01:13:07.460
The two Tories are now in the spaceship, and the cosmonauts are a lot smarter than we can be.

01:13:07.960 --> 01:13:14.930
What that means for us, and how Team 3 will react to it ...

01:13:30.760 --> 01:13:34.940
No, boss. Boss, I wanted to... Boss, I wanted to...

01:13:36.480 --> 01:13:39.230
Boss, I... No, boss, let me explain!

01:13:39.930 --> 01:13:41.700
Boss, I...

01:13:41.700 --> 01:13:47.060
You have five seconds for your answer.

01:13:47.820 --> 01:13:49.560
Boss, I have the solution.

01:13:49.760 --> 01:13:51.020
A fantastic idea.

01:13:51.180 --> 01:13:52.840
The three of them will be satisfied with it.

01:13:53.490 --> 01:13:55.190
Not... not with violence.

01:13:55.450 --> 01:13:57.170
Only... only natural forces.

01:14:02.260 --> 01:14:12.470
In the airfield there is an underground water run. We just pump it up.

01:14:12.910 --> 01:14:17.940
Before it reaches the water, they have to fly off. Otherwise, the spaceship would sink and therefore not be able to take off.

01:14:20.890 --> 01:14:25.530
So the theme was not always on your planet. Only for three generations.

01:14:25.930 --> 01:14:26.070
Yes.

01:14:26.450 --> 01:14:28.190
And always only wanted that one mineral.

01:14:30.000 --> 01:14:35.770
You had to dismantle it and you flew it to Theme 3. Did we understand you correctly? Did you do anything about it?

01:14:36.700 --> 01:14:39.820
Yes, we defended ourselves. But they are overpowered with their weapons.

01:14:40.360 --> 01:14:44.240
We alone cannot force them to leave our planet. But now ...

01:14:44.240 --> 01:14:49.600
Wait a minute. So the call for help comes from you?

01:14:49.820 --> 01:14:57.800
Yes. Two young people of ours who had to build up the big broadcasting station on the subject tried to send a call for help.

01:14:58.680 --> 01:14:59.980
But already after ...

01:15:00.000 --> 01:15:03.280
In a short time, the transmission system was blocked by something.

01:15:04.040 --> 01:15:06.340
The two were shot.

01:15:06.840 --> 01:15:09.390
We all had to watch out.

01:15:10.290 --> 01:15:11.690
They were the sons of Xig.

01:15:11.810 --> 01:15:15.840
Give us weapons, please.

01:15:16.250 --> 01:15:17.570
With you. Together.

01:15:18.180 --> 01:15:19.820
Let's chase them away from our planet.

01:15:26.080 --> 01:15:26.680
Xig is dead.

01:15:39.920 --> 01:15:43.370
So often, when we were all desperate, he gave us courage.

01:15:43.830 --> 01:15:46.520
His death will shake us all up.

01:15:46.960 --> 01:15:50.190
It's the right moment.

01:15:50.550 --> 01:15:52.850
Give us weapons.

01:15:53.030 --> 01:15:55.190
Give us weapons.

01:15:57.660 --> 01:15:58.800
Let's take it, we'll give you weapons.

01:16:00.280 --> 01:16:02.920
How long do you think it will take for Tem 3 space ships to arrive?

01:16:03.840 --> 01:16:04.140
What then?

01:16:04.340 --> 01:16:06.920
Then it will have to come from Cynro space ships.

01:16:07.300 --> 01:16:09.300
A galactic war carried out on your planet.

01:16:09.980 --> 01:16:11.040
That's nonsense.

01:16:12.020 --> 01:16:13.200
Then we have no hope.

01:16:13.500 --> 01:16:19.170
It will take so long that many of us will no longer experience it.

01:16:20.740 --> 01:16:21.240
That's bitter.

01:16:21.440 --> 01:16:22.950
For us too.

01:16:23.010 --> 01:16:28.170
But we can't build a shield around your entire planet so that you can develop undisturbed.

01:16:31.050 --> 01:16:34.830
You are very smart, Zuko. I understand every word.

01:16:36.180 --> 01:16:38.880
Nevertheless, I don't understand it.

01:16:40.560 --> 01:16:43.360
Xig, he would have understood you.

01:16:43.440 --> 01:16:47.290
He thought and spoke like you.

01:16:55.130 --> 01:16:55.290
Well?

01:16:56.020 --> 01:16:57.060
Plus one.

01:16:57.480 --> 01:16:57.920
Perfect.

01:17:00.000 --> 01:17:03.360
Akala, what are we supposed to do? Please tell me.

01:17:03.580 --> 01:17:05.660
I can't answer your question.

01:17:06.600 --> 01:17:08.020
There's only one thing I know for sure.

01:17:09.080 --> 01:17:11.640
Help doesn't just mean we're going to give you weapons.

01:17:13.840 --> 01:17:16.900
Help means a lot, a lot more.

01:17:19.170 --> 01:17:20.030
What's going on?

01:17:20.050 --> 01:17:20.830
Are we approaching the subject?

01:17:21.110 --> 01:17:21.950
Are we getting visitors?

01:17:22.290 --> 01:17:27.230
I don't understand why our radar told us to look.

01:17:27.530 --> 01:17:28.050
No movement.

01:17:28.970 --> 01:17:29.970
Maybe that's...

01:17:30.000 --> 01:17:35.570
only the ground waves. The terrain is rising to the horizon and the radar machine has

01:17:35.570 --> 01:17:42.440
included it in its range of effect. Why all of a sudden? Maybe a

01:17:42.440 --> 01:17:47.040
tiny change in the adjustment. One could almost think you are disappointed. Would you prefer

01:17:47.040 --> 01:17:54.220
the Thema to march up with its air and land forces? At least they would

01:17:54.220 --> 01:17:58.900
take a difficult decision with Acala. Wonderful, it works.

01:18:00.000 --> 01:18:01.080
Let's get to work now!

01:18:01.120 --> 01:18:02.260
Push at full speed with all your might!

01:18:02.820 --> 01:18:06.610
If we could use machines, everything would be much faster.

01:18:07.240 --> 01:18:08.160
Why don't we do that?

01:18:08.580 --> 01:18:12.110
You idiot! The machine noises are immediately recorded in the spaceship!

01:18:12.870 --> 01:18:15.840
If we stay undiscovered for just one day, one night and another day!

01:18:51.790 --> 01:18:56.090
Come and tell me about the start of the consultation.

01:18:57.290 --> 01:18:57.910
Akala, please.

01:19:00.000 --> 01:19:02.480
Everyone knows that Suko flew in because of you, because of you.

01:19:02.660 --> 01:19:05.410
Because of what?

01:19:08.410 --> 01:19:09.730
He's not a piece of shit.

01:19:10.030 --> 01:19:12.110
He's making himself as difficult as you are.

01:19:13.370 --> 01:19:15.110
History is one side.

01:19:15.330 --> 01:19:17.750
The tactical version of our approach is the other.

01:19:18.150 --> 01:19:21.610
If we really want to help Duri...

01:19:23.290 --> 01:19:25.030
Calm down.

01:19:26.230 --> 01:19:26.750
Akala.

01:19:27.190 --> 01:19:28.520
What's going on?

01:19:28.600 --> 01:19:29.880
Do you feel...

01:19:30.000 --> 01:19:31.040
We let you down.

01:19:31.060 --> 01:19:34.740
No, you're afraid to make a decision.

01:19:37.140 --> 01:19:38.440
I'll make it.

01:19:40.940 --> 01:19:42.180
Akala, I'm not satisfied with such an answer.

01:19:43.220 --> 01:19:46.360
If we want to help Ture, then what?

01:19:48.520 --> 01:19:51.880
Then we have to stay here.

01:19:52.140 --> 01:19:56.760
Stay here? You always mean to stay here.

01:19:56.980 --> 01:19:59.060
This can't be serious, Akala!

01:20:00.090 --> 01:20:02.750
Do you really mean it? Akala, do you hear me?

01:20:02.890 --> 01:20:05.200
Stay here. Stay here forever.

01:20:05.400 --> 01:20:06.620
I heard you right.

01:20:08.060 --> 01:20:10.140
Our mission can't be understood like this.

01:20:12.160 --> 01:20:18.740
Besides, such a plan is hopeless. Absurd.

01:20:38.510 --> 01:20:43.200
It doesn't matter if we stay here forever, after a certain amount of time being eliminated by another Synro team.

01:20:44.000 --> 01:20:50.560
It's all about a confrontation between them and Synro. Don't you see that?

01:20:50.900 --> 01:20:59.900
So your conclusion is that a war can only be prevented by our departure. Our soon departure.

01:21:00.000 --> 01:21:06.370
When we wanted to fly away, when we wanted to fly away from this mental blockade,

01:21:07.810 --> 01:21:09.780
you forced us to stay here because of your excursions.

01:21:10.780 --> 01:21:14.220
At this point in time, I didn't know anything about the Turis.

01:21:14.440 --> 01:21:16.160
The return flight seemed necessary to me.

01:21:16.160 --> 01:21:20.760
But now that we know the situation of the Turis, it is impossible for me to fly away.

01:21:21.740 --> 01:21:29.870
What do you think of a laser at Cynode?

01:21:30.000 --> 01:21:34.230
send and ask what you think of it. After all, you are not only a member of the expedition,

01:21:34.610 --> 01:21:44.160
but the commander. The decision can only be made here, not on Zynro. Any

01:21:44.160 --> 01:21:53.940
instructions, commander? Zuko, did you really just fly with me?

01:22:06.880 --> 01:22:09.470
You didn't convince the others, is that clear to you?

01:22:09.470 --> 01:22:15.400
The others? Why do you assume that?

01:22:15.960 --> 01:22:26.000
Listen Akala, if you stay with your decision, I'll make use of my right as a board doctor.

01:22:26.460 --> 01:22:29.620
I will suggest a different...

01:22:30.000 --> 01:22:34.610
to transfer the command from us with the order to resume the expedition.

01:22:35.700 --> 01:22:38.200
After a very thorough radio contact with Synro.

01:22:39.860 --> 01:22:43.120
If that is your opinion, then you are obliged to do so.

01:22:47.920 --> 01:22:48.920
I'm not crazy.

01:22:50.820 --> 01:22:53.020
I don't care how another commander would act on my behalf.

01:22:53.740 --> 01:22:58.520
I have to do what I think is necessary.

01:23:00.220 --> 01:23:04.340
I have checked the radar surveillance adjustment. It is not adjusted.

01:23:04.800 --> 01:23:08.620
Would you make a radio connection with the central station for me?

01:23:08.740 --> 01:23:11.230
Let the boss give it to me. Right now.

01:23:11.720 --> 01:23:14.160
The crew is not locked behind me.

01:23:14.300 --> 01:23:16.260
Maybe I can find a way out.

01:23:16.920 --> 01:23:18.930
Not to stay here.

01:23:19.090 --> 01:23:21.110
Do you agree with that?

01:23:21.590 --> 01:23:22.920
Yes, I am.

01:23:23.300 --> 01:23:24.640
Where do you want to meet him?

01:23:25.280 --> 01:23:26.880
I hope you'll fly me with the probe.

01:23:50.160 --> 01:23:52.160
Don't do that! That way we'll never be finished!

01:23:52.360 --> 01:23:55.800
Drive it right! The pump must stop when the exhaust of the dustbin is finished!

01:23:56.100 --> 01:23:57.520
Don't be so timid, speed up the steam!

01:24:00.440 --> 01:24:14.730
I hear.

01:24:16.180 --> 01:24:19.140
Boss, the reported probe is on the way. What should we do?

01:24:20.070 --> 01:24:22.770
Lead the commander immediately after landing in my park.

01:24:23.010 --> 01:24:29.170
How far has Ronk come?

01:24:30.670 --> 01:24:33.710
The transport columns with the pump parts have arrived at the construction site.

01:24:34.860 --> 01:24:38.330
Boss, everything is going according to Ron's plan.

01:24:38.670 --> 01:24:38.930
Won.

01:24:54.220 --> 01:24:54.720
Won.

01:24:56.600 --> 01:24:57.200
WON!

01:25:01.150 --> 01:25:01.410
YAH!

01:25:02.540 --> 01:25:23.640
If you want to go to the robber cage, I want to listen to you at least.

01:25:23.640 --> 01:25:25.680
Don't let the best of you fall on you.

01:25:25.680 --> 01:25:28.610
Let's go.

01:25:29.020 --> 01:25:29.340
One.

01:25:30.600 --> 01:25:32.360
Two, three...

01:25:32.360 --> 01:25:36.500
If I give you a signal, you have to go back immediately.

01:25:37.150 --> 01:25:37.550
I promise.

01:26:44.970 --> 01:26:47.690
I'm happy that we can continue our conversation that we had to interrupt so unluckily.

01:26:48.690 --> 01:26:52.930
I hope music doesn't bother you.

01:26:53.230 --> 01:26:55.510
I need distraction if I want to concentrate.

01:28:04.510 --> 01:28:06.170
I thought a lot about them, my dear.

01:28:06.450 --> 01:28:08.570
You Zynro people, what kind of people are you?

01:28:08.570 --> 01:28:11.590
What drives you through the galaxy?

01:28:12.450 --> 01:28:14.330
Which laws determine your actions?

01:28:15.510 --> 01:28:18.720
Our first law says, no one should suppress another.

01:28:19.700 --> 01:28:26.490
A nice thought. But the Thuris have no culture, you see.

01:28:27.420 --> 01:28:29.960
When they left our planet and went home...

01:28:30.000 --> 01:28:35.640
way, then it won't take long and the turi believe they have dreamed

01:28:35.640 --> 01:28:41.900
gods rose from heaven they were friendly and they disappeared again they

01:28:43.340 --> 01:28:46.670
will perhaps pray to these gods and their modest life will

01:28:46.670 --> 01:28:54.940
get a little shine through it no longer and that's a lot i hope you

01:28:54.940 --> 01:28:58.100
have brought some time for me it is clapping so pleasantly

01:29:34.160 --> 01:29:35.680
I hear the thought of brotherhood.

01:29:35.960 --> 01:29:39.420
For me, only one law applies, the power.

01:29:50.710 --> 01:29:54.740
But now you have to hurry.

01:29:55.400 --> 01:29:58.950
Why? I don't understand.

01:30:00.000 --> 01:30:01.400
Your great time is coming to an end.

01:30:02.000 --> 01:30:03.240
Isn't that clear to you?

01:30:03.240 --> 01:30:07.000
The secret of your planet is no longer a secret.

01:30:07.500 --> 01:30:08.420
This is the first step.

01:30:09.060 --> 01:30:09.820
The first step?

01:30:10.040 --> 01:30:13.270
Where to?

01:30:13.390 --> 01:30:16.170
Did I scare you with it?

01:30:17.240 --> 01:30:17.920
Oh, I didn't want that.

01:30:21.600 --> 01:30:27.680
What is...

01:30:27.680 --> 01:30:28.740
What happened?

01:30:34.540 --> 01:30:36.120
I'm making you a suggestion, an offer.

01:30:36.360 --> 01:30:39.480
Stay on Theme 4.

01:30:39.740 --> 01:30:43.620
And you really think you'd be happy with me?

01:30:44.750 --> 01:30:48.070
You're intelligent.

01:30:48.450 --> 01:30:50.420
If you follow the rules.

01:30:51.100 --> 01:30:51.620
Certainly.

01:31:00.000 --> 01:31:05.220
Yes, I understand you. Rule number one. What is above stays above.

01:31:06.240 --> 01:31:11.550
And rule number two. Those who are below, they stay below.

01:31:12.900 --> 01:31:18.960
That's exactly how it is and so it stays. Or do you want to give Tori weapons?

01:31:20.090 --> 01:31:23.560
Apparently you can only think in the forms of the most primitive violence.

01:31:26.180 --> 01:31:29.970
Try to follow my thoughts. Your coexistence...

01:31:30.000 --> 01:31:31.260
On the planet of the Turi is...

01:31:31.260 --> 01:31:31.760
Turi planet?

01:31:32.140 --> 01:31:33.500
He belongs to us!

01:31:33.700 --> 01:31:35.960
We have conquered him!

01:31:39.320 --> 01:31:39.940
Expel us!

01:31:40.120 --> 01:31:42.560
He has flown out of the center.

01:31:43.200 --> 01:31:45.960
She reports, Thema is preparing to flood our launch pad.

01:31:46.360 --> 01:31:47.560
Got it.

01:32:00.060 --> 01:32:04.870
A message from ZB-3, one of the Turi-girls, the Ch'ta, has flown out of the headquarters.

01:32:05.450 --> 01:32:07.300
What should we do?

01:32:07.500 --> 01:32:26.100
And forget about him, if he exists!

01:32:31.240 --> 01:32:33.500
Ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha!

01:32:34.220 --> 01:32:36.760
Here comes a sun of the Zündroh, folks!

01:32:37.180 --> 01:32:44.860
The Torii over there!

01:32:44.940 --> 01:32:46.710
Then the pump as tight as possible!

01:32:46.990 --> 01:32:47.210
Come on!

01:33:10.630 --> 01:33:13.990
Distance of the water mirror to the flood point maybe 30 cm.

01:33:14.820 --> 01:33:16.760
Akala, we have to set up the pump right away.

01:33:17.140 --> 01:33:22.790
If you want to buy the life of 500 turis, they have driven the subject close to the pump.

01:33:24.080 --> 01:33:25.260
Order alarm start.

01:33:25.670 --> 01:33:26.730
Understood, alarm start.

01:33:27.420 --> 01:33:28.560
Alarm start.

01:33:30.250 --> 01:33:33.640
This is the 110.

01:33:35.150 --> 01:33:37.230
Please, the title.

01:33:40.050 --> 01:33:43.620
Akala, Suko, get us out of here immediately.

01:33:46.860 --> 01:33:48.240
Akala, this is K'teh.

01:33:48.380 --> 01:33:51.100
The pump must be put out of operation.

01:33:51.700 --> 01:33:53.560
We will help you.

01:33:54.040 --> 01:33:55.320
Otherwise you can't do it.

01:33:55.440 --> 01:33:57.000
We want to talk to our people.

01:33:58.620 --> 01:33:59.060
We're coming.

01:34:02.240 --> 01:34:02.280
...

01:34:06.010 --> 01:34:06.430
Boss?

01:34:09.980 --> 01:34:10.240
Boss!

01:34:11.400 --> 01:34:15.930
A probe of the Zünder people has dropped two turrets at the construction site.

01:34:16.630 --> 01:34:24.880
Give me Ronk, and I want to listen to the radio connection to the spaceship.

01:34:25.600 --> 01:34:29.750
I'll be right back!

01:34:30.000 --> 01:34:31.950
Get back, you damn guys, or you'll be shot!

01:34:32.350 --> 01:34:37.100
We can't do the pumping work, but we're delaying the water.

01:34:37.260 --> 01:34:38.980
Hurry up with the start!

01:34:39.470 --> 01:34:41.570
Ronk, the boss wants to talk to you.

01:34:41.590 --> 01:34:43.160
I'm listening.

01:34:44.230 --> 01:34:47.010
Don't lose your head. Leave the little ones alone.

01:34:47.830 --> 01:34:50.700
First the spaceship has to start and disappear.

01:34:51.750 --> 01:34:54.330
Then you can feed your goldfish with the turis.

01:34:54.490 --> 01:34:58.670
But now you have to concentrate on everything?

01:35:00.220 --> 01:35:01.020
You didn't understand the abflug.

01:35:02.000 --> 01:35:05.050
The breakthrough is not being worked on.

01:35:05.500 --> 01:35:06.660
Ronk, come quickly!

01:35:07.900 --> 01:35:08.380
Ronk!

01:35:09.120 --> 01:35:10.800
Ronk threw the radio on the floor.

01:35:18.530 --> 01:35:19.870
Yes, you moron, I hear.

01:35:20.810 --> 01:35:23.270
Come on, boss. The breakthrough is about to be blown up.

01:35:23.270 --> 01:35:24.580
Did you understand? Repeat.

01:35:26.180 --> 01:35:29.900
Understood. The breakthrough is about to be blown up, but...

01:35:30.250 --> 01:35:31.070
What's wrong with Ronk?

01:35:31.070 --> 01:35:32.980
Leave it to the boss.

01:35:33.180 --> 01:35:37.510
How far are you? Hurry up! We can't take any longer!

01:36:39.880 --> 01:36:40.220
Get in touch.

01:36:41.530 --> 01:36:41.970
Zuko?

01:36:42.420 --> 01:36:43.260
What's going on?

01:36:43.620 --> 01:36:44.720
I have a stomach ache.

01:36:45.700 --> 01:36:47.680
I only have half a minute left until ignition.

01:36:47.860 --> 01:36:48.440
Hurry up!

01:36:49.610 --> 01:36:50.050
Zuko?

01:36:50.070 --> 01:36:51.620
What happened?

01:36:52.560 --> 01:36:52.960
Zuko!

01:36:53.680 --> 01:36:54.120
Zuko!

01:36:54.160 --> 01:36:56.910
Help me!

01:36:57.800 --> 01:36:59.260
The water is running!

01:37:00.320 --> 01:37:01.120
Everything according to plan.

01:37:01.440 --> 01:37:04.320
And I missed a thought-tank for this guy.

01:37:06.800 --> 01:37:09.090
This weak-headed.

01:37:10.620 --> 01:37:10.980
This...

01:37:10.980 --> 01:37:15.300
This damned...

01:37:15.490 --> 01:37:16.110
...Akala!

01:37:16.330 --> 01:37:18.050
We'll get the whole Turin back!

01:37:18.170 --> 01:37:19.220
We'll get it back!

01:40:00.000 --> 01:40:00.200
Thank you.
